<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Antanosy</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Antanosy people</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Antanosy are a Malagasy people of the Anosy region in south-eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/madagascar">Madagascar</a>, around <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/taolagnaro">Taolagnaro</a> (Fort-Dauphin). From around 1500 they were ruled by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zafiraminia">Zafiraminia</a>, a clan claiming Muslim origins, and in 1643 French settlers founded Fort-Dauphin in their land. Conflicts with the settlers ended the French colony in 1674.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/antanosy.jpg" alt="Antanosy" width="320" height="434" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown author. · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Two_Antanosy_,men,_1900-1910.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
